# AWS CCP — Storage & Databases

Which service stores objects in buckets with virtually unlimited capacity?
---
S3
= Amazon S3
= Simple Storage Service
---
Objects up to 5 TB, addressed by key. Not a filesystem and not attachable to an instance.

S3 is designed for {{11}} nines (99.999999999%) of durability.
---
Durability is about not losing the object. Availability, which varies by storage class, is about reaching it now.

Which S3 storage class automatically moves objects between access tiers based on usage?
---
Intelligent-Tiering
~ Standard-IA
~ One Zone-IA
~ Glacier Flexible Retrieval
---
For data with unpredictable access patterns. A small monitoring fee replaces guessing.

Which S3 storage class is the cheapest for archives you can wait about 12 hours to retrieve?
---
Glacier Deep Archive
~ Glacier Instant Retrieval
~ Standard-IA
~ One Zone-IA
---
The lowest-cost storage on AWS. Think compliance archives kept for years.

Which S3 storage class offers archive-level pricing with millisecond retrieval?
---
Glacier Instant Retrieval
~ Glacier Flexible Retrieval
~ Glacier Deep Archive
~ Standard
---
For data touched about once a quarter. Flexible Retrieval takes minutes to hours instead.

S3 {{lifecycle}} rules transition objects to cheaper storage classes or expire them on a schedule.
---
Standard to Standard-IA to Glacier to deletion, all automatic.

Which service provides block storage volumes that attach to EC2 instances?
---
EBS
= Amazon EBS
= Elastic Block Store
---
A volume lives in one Availability Zone. Snapshots go to S3 and cross that boundary.

What happens to data on an instance store when the instance stops?
---
It is lost
~ It persists until deleted
~ It is snapshotted automatically
~ It moves to S3
---
Instance store is ephemeral disk physically attached to the host. Use EBS for anything durable.

Which service provides a shared network file system that many Linux instances can mount at once?
---
EFS
= Amazon EFS
= Elastic File System
---
NFS, grows and shrinks automatically, spans multiple AZs.

Which service gives Windows servers a native SMB file share?
---
FSx for Windows File Server
= Amazon FSx
= FSx
---
The FSx family also covers Lustre for high-performance computing.

Which hybrid service gives on-premises applications access to cloud storage?
---
Storage Gateway
= AWS Storage Gateway
---
File, volume, and tape flavors. The tape one replaces physical backup tapes with S3.

Which family of rugged physical devices ships your data to AWS when the network is too slow?
---
Snowball
= AWS Snowball
= Snowball Edge
= Snow family
---
Weeks of uploading become a courier trip. Snowball Edge also runs compute at remote sites.

Which managed service runs relational engines like MySQL and PostgreSQL, handling backups and patching for you?
---
RDS
= Amazon RDS
= Relational Database Service
---
Also MariaDB, Oracle, and SQL Server. You tune the database, AWS turns the wrenches.

Which AWS-built relational database is MySQL- and PostgreSQL-compatible with several times the throughput?
---
Aurora
= Amazon Aurora
---
Storage replicates six ways across three AZs. Aurora Serverless scales capacity on demand.

What does an RDS Multi-AZ deployment provide?
---
A standby replica that takes over automatically if the primary fails
~ Faster read performance
~ A cheaper storage tier
~ Cross-region disaster recovery
---
For read scaling you want read replicas instead. Multi-AZ is purely about availability.

Which serverless NoSQL key-value database delivers single-digit-millisecond performance at any scale?
---
DynamoDB
= Amazon DynamoDB
---
No servers, no capacity ceiling. DAX adds an in-memory cache for microseconds.

Which service adds an in-memory cache using Redis or Memcached?
---
ElastiCache
= Amazon ElastiCache
---
Put it in front of a database to absorb hot reads.

Which petabyte-scale data warehouse runs analytical SQL queries?
---
Redshift
= Amazon Redshift
---
Analytics over huge historical datasets. RDS is for transactions, Redshift for analysis.

Which AWS database is purpose-built for graphs and highly connected data?
---
Neptune
~ DynamoDB
~ DocumentDB
~ Redshift
---
Social networks, recommendations, fraud rings.

Amazon DocumentDB is compatible with which database API?
---
MongoDB
~ Cassandra
~ Redis
~ Oracle
---
Amazon Keyspaces is the Cassandra-compatible sibling.

Which service migrates databases to AWS with minimal downtime?
---
DMS
= AWS DMS
= Database Migration Service
---
The source stays live during migration. It can also convert between engines with SCT.

Which service centralizes and automates backups across AWS services?
---
Backup
= AWS Backup
---
One policy covering EBS, RDS, DynamoDB, EFS, and more, with retention rules.
